The comparison held 7 KB of locals (the old kit's copy drawers) plus 850
bytes in emit_copy; run from the Installer on its own stack that overran
into an address error (Software Failure 80000004) whenever the manifests
differed. Measured on the rig (68060): 9458 bytes of stack before, 1426
after; a 4096-byte stack crashed the old binary, the new one runs every
case. Host test measures the stack the call touches.

Install: stop with a message when a volume named UP-Term is mounted (it
clashes with the UP-Term: assign).
